% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `standard_editor` (Pmacs's
% editor object), compiled by psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.
% It is NOT SIMPOS: no part of it is printed.  It is MINIMAL: of the
% selectors held code sends to an editor (docs/simpos/subsystems/
% window.md §2.11 and its usage table: get_window/2, current_buffer/2,
% set_current_buffer/2, select_buffer/2, clear_input/1, exception/2,
% carriage_return/1, ...) only get_window/2 is here, because 21 methods
% of pimfep##pimos_window_editor stop at it (kl0 census --fep,
% 2026-11-24).  pimos_window_editor's natures, as its template writes
% them, are `simpos##standard_editor, pimfep##as_pimos_device`, so this
% is the unloaded ancestor that holds the method (the other one,
% simpos##as_program, is reached through as_pimos_device).
%
% Model (OURS): the editor's window in one slot.  In SIMPOS the window
% and its editor are made together by `:create(#pmacs_window, Opts, _, W)`
% and `:get_editor(W, E)` (window.md §2.11, from disc/exshow.esp:23-35);
% class pmacs_window is not stood in, so no window is ever made and the
% slot keeps its constant 0.  kl0 then refuses the next send, to the
% window, as "receiver not an object".

class standard_editor has

instance

% INTERPOLATED: the representation (OURS; see above).
attribute window := 0;

% :get_window(Editor, Window) -- the editor's window.
% INTERPOLATED from: window.md §2.11 ("editor -> window", 188 uses);
% the call sites kappa2 utility/fmp/KMACS.ESP:84, :106 and others
% (`:get_window(Editor,Window)`, then window methods on Window); the held
% compiled sends in pimfep##pimos_window_editor (21 methods, 2026-11-24).
:get_window(Editor, Window) :- Window = Editor!window;

end.
